comments[12]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T15:40:12.258Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: custom-type completeness aggregation, bounded diagnostic examples, counts-only projection, CLI strict-exit negative control and remediation pass. The report and lifecycle write enforcement share the same require_fields evaluator. Public documentation now has a reachable index entry. Related implementation dependency is recorded on pm-mj42og."
  "2026-09-08T16:24:43.390Z","harness:codex","Verification: the linked sandboxed completeness checks pass, including custom types, bounded examples, counts-only projection, explicit refusal under strict-exit, and remediation to a clean result. The shared policy suite also passes and default validate includes completeness. No default policies are installed into existing trackers."
  "2026-09-08T16:50:58.717Z","harness:codex","Final implementation evidence: Linked completeness tests pass for custom types, counts-only output, refusal and remediation. The full 8615-test run passes with exact 100/100/100/100 source coverage; manual strict completeness validation passes."
  "2026-09-08T18:20:14.151Z","harness:codex","Third-round TDD: the existing unknown-author scenario failed after adding an assertion that completeness remains ok. Capture item-read incompleteness immediately after reading items, before unrelated history advice is appended. The fix preserves fail-closed behavior for unreadable item sources."
  "2026-09-08T18:31:49.458Z","harness:codex","Third-round verification: full 8620-test coverage passes at exact 100/100/100/100. Real unknown-author history advice no longer marks completeness as an incomplete source; a malformed item file still produces an error. A separate compiled CLI run in a temporary tracker preserved validate_history_unknown_author_events:1 while reporting completeness status ok."
  "2026-09-08T18:35:21.923Z","harness:codex","Final third-round evidence: Completeness now derives source validity only from item-read diagnostics and preserves unrelated history advice. Full suite: 8620 tests in 652 files passed with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. After the one-use metadata initializer was inlined, all 137 focused validation/attribution/contract tests and the direct static gate passed. All linked tests, manual CLI acceptance, typecheck, generated contracts, secret scan and zero-vulnerability dependency audit passed. Full current-head hosted review and preflight remain merge requirements."
  "2026-09-08T21:35:01.279Z","harness:codex","Sixth-round correction: completeness creates one private policy evaluator for the whole corpus, avoiding repeated declaration serialization and SHA-256 work. The snapshot regression fails before the new API and passes afterward, including caller mutation and fresh evaluator behavior."
  "2026-09-08T21:57:57.834Z","harness:codex","Sixth-round verification: all 8622 tests in 653 files pass with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and zero uncovered statements, branches, functions and lines. All four TypeScript projects, the full quality:static gate, serialized docs/skills checks, and every linked test command pass. Both original clone profiles remain unchanged; the supplementary historical-table profile also passes. Final pushed-head CI, full platform matrix, review and preflight remain required before merge."
  "2026-09-08T22:55:32.129Z","harness:codex","Seventh-round TDD: malformed policy JSON first aborted default validate with workflow_policy_registry_invalid. The completeness module now contains only policy-read failures in an error check with a relative registry path and repair hint; independent diagnostics continue. Real SDK/CLI regressions cover malformed JSON, invalid declarations, invalid UTF-8 and a directory storage fault without changing policy bytes or item history. A separate temporary CLI run preserves all ten default validation checks, exits 1 on corruption and exits 0 after repair. Final 8623 tests in 653 files pass at exact 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts (63729 statements, 48461 branches, 13216 functions, 61134 lines). All four TypeScript projects, direct structural/docstring gate, focused ESLint, linked tests, docs gate, public SDK/contracts snapshots and all three clone profiles pass. The helper stays in the existing completeness module to retain unchanged file-length and complexity ceilings. The preceding bfb737b4b full preflight and Nightly attempt 2 passed; the initial macOS kill EPERM did not reproduce on the unchanged failed-job retry. Final pushed-head CI, full platform validation and review remain merge requirements."
  "2026-09-09T00:59:23.869Z","harness:codex","Full review of bdcd47a found that state completeness arbitrarily supplies update and therefore treats update-only requirements differently from close/import-only requirements. The correction explicitly excludes all operation-scoped declarations from state completeness, preserves exact mutation matching and reports the state-only scope. The preceding full preflight passed; Nightly 34294922496 passed after an unchanged Windows failed-job retry of an intermittent nested HTTP startup timeout. No timeout or source suppression was applied."
  "2026-09-09T01:03:04.077Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: both new regressions failed against bdcd47a; the state report included update-evidence and reported two violations instead of one. With the shared evaluator excluding operation-scoped policies, focused unit and SDK/CLI regressions pass. Exact operation matching still refuses a real close after state evidence is supplied. The scan advertises operation_independent_require_fields and the public docs describe that scope. All four TypeScript projects pass; full coverage and static verification are running."
  "2026-09-09T01:11:16.373Z","harness:codex","Final operation-scope correction evidence: Full 8625-test coverage in 653 files passes at exact 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered counts: 63729 statements, 48462 branches, 13216 functions and 61134 lines. All four TypeScript projects, direct structural/docstring assurance, focused ESLint, public SDK and command snapshots, graph composition and both linked test commands pass. Independent temporary CLI acceptance reports one state requirement, repairs to success, then correctly refuses an operation-specific close while preserving item history."
